WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:04.600
Safety regions, planners and trainers all face the same question:

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.329
which situations should we prepare for?

3
00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:13.696
Scenario Spark helps you explore plausible scenarios for exercises, incident preparation and policy decisions.

4
00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:18.862
It uses morphological analysis, also known as the Zwicky box.

5
00:00:18.912 --> 00:00:25.675
You list the key factors of a situation, each with a few possible values.

6
00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:32.001
A scenario picks one value per factor, and inconsistent combinations are left out.

7
00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:37.284
In this tutorial, Scenario Spark and an AI assistant work together.

8
00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:41.813
With a single prompt, you get a title, a narrative,

9
00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:47.249
a reflection on every course of action, and feedback from every persona.

10
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.803
We start from the starter kit, and choose the scenario type Event safety.

11
00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.546
Open Create scenario.

12
00:00:55.596 --> 00:01:00.356
This box contains measures, so we turn on decision support.

13
00:01:00.707 --> 00:01:01.612
Click Generate.

14
00:01:01.662 --> 00:01:07.344
Spark picks a consistent option for every factor, and summarises the situation.

15
00:01:07.695 --> 00:01:10.531
Estimate the risk if nobody acts:

16
00:01:10.581 --> 00:01:13.898
a medium probability, with a high impact.

17
00:01:14.248 --> 00:01:36.779
Next, choose the measures for course of action A, and estimate the risk that remains.

18
00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:45.201
Duplicate it as course of action B, and change a few measures:

19
00:01:45.251 --> 00:01:52.646
a casualty collection point, a joint coordination team, and phased departure.

20
00:01:52.996 --> 00:01:54.789
Now click Ask LLM.

21
00:01:54.839 --> 00:01:59.859
Spark builds one combined prompt that asks for everything at once,

22
00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:03.546
and copies it to your clipboard straight away.

23
00:02:03.896 --> 00:02:11.403
So you can paste it directly into your AI assistant, for example Copilot in Microsoft Edge.

24
00:02:11.753 --> 00:02:18.447
The assistant answers with a single JSON block.

25
00:02:18.497 --> 00:02:20.976
Copy the answer.

26
00:02:21.327 --> 00:02:24.042
Paste the JSON into the dialog.

27
00:02:24.092 --> 00:02:28.652
Spark checks it, and shows a preview of every part.

28
00:02:28.702 --> 00:02:31.878
Untick anything you don't want to use.

29
00:02:32.228 --> 00:02:33.167
Click Apply.

30
00:02:33.217 --> 00:02:37.125
The narrative is saved under the suggested title.

31
00:02:37.475 --> 00:02:39.308
Review the result.

32
00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:42.447
The narrative remains fully editable.

33
00:02:42.797 --> 00:02:49.797
Each course of action now has its own reflection.

34
00:02:50.147 --> 00:02:54.611
And every persona describes how they experience the situation.

35
00:02:54.961 --> 00:02:59.994
Tick Select for analysis to add it to your saved scenarios.

36
00:03:00.044 --> 00:03:05.077
Now it also counts in the box and in decision support.

37
00:03:05.427 --> 00:03:10.739
In the morphological box, each category has its own tab.

38
00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:16.638
Coloured options show how often they are used in saved scenarios.

39
00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:22.756
The decision support page puts the courses of action side by side.

40
00:03:23.106 --> 00:03:32.576
Compare their measures, and see how each course of action lowers the risk in the risk matrix.

41
00:03:32.926 --> 00:03:47.653
Finally, record your decision and its rationale in the decision log.

42
00:03:48.004 --> 00:03:55.076
Back on the home page, the saved scenario is ready to view, compare, or export.

43
00:03:55.427 --> 00:03:58.091
Want to redo just one part?

44
00:03:58.141 --> 00:04:02.163
Turn on Prompt per field in the LLM settings.

45
00:04:02.213 --> 00:04:08.497
Next to the all-in-one prompt, you then get a separate prompt for the narrative,

46
00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.759
each reflection, and each persona.

47
00:04:11.109 --> 00:04:11.970
That's it:

48
00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:16.980
from morphological box to a complete scenario in a few minutes.

49
00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:18.802
Now try it yourself.

50
00:04:18.852 --> 00:04:24.268
Scenario Spark runs in your browser, and the link is on screen.
